{"question_id": "q03-terrain-slope", "run": 1, "cache": "cold", "status": "ok", "error": null, "latency_s": 15.45, "provenance": {"at": "2026-10-19T23:44:53.917Z", "turn_id": "turn_0bda1309", "session_id": "4eadee079bd0", "subject": "anonymous", "model": "eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5", "models_used": ["eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5"], "prompt_version": "a9f7e88fc432", "memory_context": false, "sdk": "pydantic-ai-slim 2.54.0", "tools_called": ["geocode", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "render_object"], "num_turns": 5, "duration_ms": 15185, "duration_api_ms": null, "total_cost_usd": 0.02435576, "usage": {"input_tokens": 12, "output_tokens": 1258, "cache_read_input_tokens": 42351, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2121}, "is_error": false, "retried_fresh": false, "refused": false, "error": null, "http_status": null, "runtime": "pydantic-ai", "provider": "bedrock", "cost_source": "genai-prices 0.1.13 (regional.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5)"}, "images": 1, "files": 0, "answer": "I analysed a 600 \u00d7 600 m area around Chalmers (EPSG:3006 bounds 319200\u2013319800 E, 6397700\u20136398300 N). I used a 2 m DEM built from 412,446 ground-classified lidar points. The 3D terrain mesh render shows the terrain shape only. It doesn't show the slope field.\n\n**Elevation**\n- Range: about 41 m to 87 m, so about 46 m of relief.\n- Mean: 61.4 m. Median: 62.2 m.\n- The 5th to 95th percentile range is 46.5 m to 75.0 m.\n\n**Slope**\nThe tool returned slope in radians. I assumed that from the aspect values, which span \u00b1\u03c0, and converted to degrees.\n\n| Statistic | Radians | Degrees |\n|---|---|---|\n| Median | 0.074 | about 4.2\u00b0 |\n| Mean | 0.154 | about 8.8\u00b0 |\n| 95th percentile | 0.553 | about 31.7\u00b0 |\n| Max | 1.29 | about 74\u00b0 |\n\n**Interpretation**\n- Most of the area is gentle. Half of the cells are under about 4\u00b0 and the mean is under 9\u00b0.\n- The mean is about twice the median, so the distribution is skewed. About 5% of cells are steeper than about 32\u00b0. Those cells are likely rock outcrops or cuttings, and the highest values may be DEM artefacts near building edges or walls.\n- The slope and aspect rasters have no location breakdown in the summary, so I can't say where the steep areas are.\n\nThe slope raster is `obj_5ea862f0` and the aspect raster is `obj_b1780f05`. I can export them as GeoTIFF or CSV. I can also re-run at a finer cell size, such as 1 m, or on a smaller area.", "operations": [{"at": "2026-10-19T23:44:40.322Z", "turn_id": "turn_0bda1309", "session_id": "4eadee079bd0", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "geocode", "operation": null, "params_hash": "ad5faefbe482eb39", "seconds": 0.003, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": [], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:44:41.461Z", "turn_id": "turn_0bda1309", "session_id": "4eadee079bd0", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "60eb5c049e03b34b", "seconds": 0.035, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": true, "object_refs": ["obj_11ae671e"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:44:44.980Z", "turn_id": "turn_0bda1309", "session_id": "4eadee079bd0", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "builder.build_terrain_raster", "params_hash": "a1dc0a98f8abb03d", "seconds": 0.127, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_61566c6b"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:44:45.146Z", "turn_id": "turn_0bda1309", "session_id": "4eadee079bd0", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "builder.build_terrain_surface_mesh", "params_hash": "6a128685772081eb", "seconds": 0.29, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["