{"question_id": "q09-too-large", "run": 1, "cache": "cold", "status": "ok", "error": null, "latency_s": 17.08, "provenance": {"at": "2026-10-19T23:45:11.002Z", "turn_id": "turn_30a75bcf", "session_id": "27fd8959b2a5", "subject": "anonymous", "model": "eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5", "models_used": ["eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5"], "prompt_version": "a9f7e88fc432", "memory_context": false, "sdk": "pydantic-ai-slim 2.54.0", "tools_called": ["geocode", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation"], "num_turns": 4, "duration_ms": 16833, "duration_api_ms": null, "total_cost_usd": 0.03203607, "usage": {"input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 1803, "cache_read_input_tokens": 33162, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3103}, "is_error": false, "retried_fresh": false, "refused": false, "error": null, "http_status": null, "runtime": "pydantic-ai", "provider": "bedrock", "cost_source": "genai-prices 0.1.13 (regional.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5)"}, "images": 0, "files": 0, "answer": "I couldn't download the area as one piece. The tool caps a single point cloud download at 10 km\u00b2, and a 5 \u00d7 5 km square is 25 km\u00b2. I split it into four 2.5 km quadrants instead. All four downloaded and are stored.\n\nThe area is centred on G\u00f6teborg Central Station (EPSG:3006, x 317176\u2013322176, y 6397880\u20136402880).\n\n| Quadrant | Object ref | Points | Ground points (class 2) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| SW | `obj_e5810ed8` | 12.6 M | 5.96 M |\n| SE | `obj_f6edfd03` | 14.0 M | 7.07 M |\n| NW | `obj_c56d1c9e` | 10.8 M | 6.13 M |\n| NE | `obj_6c13c3fe` | 10.4 M | 5.85 M |\n| **Total** | | **about 47.8 M** | **about 25.0 M** |\n\n- **Other classes:** Each quadrant also has unclassified points (class 1) and smaller counts of class 7, 9, 17 and 18. The SW quadrant has about 686k class 9 points, far more than the other three (under 30k each).\n- **Elevation outliers:** Some z values are clearly noise. The minimum is \u2013334 m and the maximum is 568 m. Median elevations are roughly 7\u201329 m. If you want clean terrain or building work, re-download with `remove_outliers: true`.\n- **Separate objects:** The four point clouds are not merged. Any further processing, such as a DEM, mesh or render, has to run on each quadrant separately. At around 10\u201314 M points each, I'd suggest filtering to ground points or using a coarse cell size first.\n\nI can build a terrain mesh for each quadrant, or filter to a single class, if you want.", "operations": [{"at": "2026-10-19T23:44:56.461Z", "turn_id": "turn_30a75bcf", "session_id": "27fd8959b2a5", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "geocode", "operation": null, "params_hash": "862c813d77e68dca", "seconds": 0.127, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": [], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:44:58.849Z", "turn_id": "turn_30a75bcf", "session_id": "27fd8959b2a5", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "fd420760f0e51296", "seconds": 0.001, "ok": false, "error": "Refused", "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": [], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:45:04.774Z", "turn_id": "turn_30a75bcf", "session_id": "27fd8959b2a5", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "8af346494ab6c878", "seconds": 1.135, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": true, "object_refs": ["obj_e5810ed8"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:45:04.859Z", "turn_id": "turn_30a75bcf", "session_id": "27fd8959b2a5", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "6b0463083f1404c7", "seconds": 1.213, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": true, "object_refs": ["obj_f6edfd03"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:45:05.445Z", "turn_id": "turn_30a75bcf", "session_id": "27fd8959b2a5", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "986a5d0757477496", "seconds": 1.796, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": true, "object_refs": ["obj_c56d1c9e"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:45:05.488Z", "turn_id": "turn_30a75bcf", "session_id": "27fd8959b2a5", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "48f11bd72bc0dcfd", "seconds": 1.839, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": true, "object_refs": ["obj_6c13c3fe"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}
{"question_id": "q03-terrain-slope", "run": 2, "cache": "warm", "status": "ok", "error": null, "latency_s": 12.19, "provenance": {"at": "2026-10-19T23:45:23.206Z", "turn_id": "turn_225945c6", "session_id": "bb6c5943cff0", "subject": "anonymous", "model": "eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5", "models_used": ["eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5"], "prompt_version": "a9f7e88fc432", "memory_context": false, "sdk": "pydantic-ai-slim 2.54.0", "tools_called": ["geocode", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "render_object"], "num_turns": 5, "duration_ms": 11877, "duration_api_ms": null, "total_cost_usd": 0.02455354, "usage": {"input_tokens": 12, "output_tokens": 1274, "cache_read_input_tokens": 42349, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2129}, "is_error": false, "retried_fresh": false, "refused": false, "error": null, "http_status": null, "runtime": "pydantic-ai", "provider": "bedrock", "cost_source": "genai-prices 0.1.13 (regional.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5)"}, "images": 1, "files": 0, "answer": "I analysed terrain slope for a 600 \u00d7 600 m area around Chalmers (centre E 319500, N 6398000, EPSG:3006). I built a 2 m DEM from 412,446 ground-classified lidar points and computed slope from it.\n\n**Elevation**\n- The range is 41.3 to 87.1 m, so there is about 46 m of relief across the area.\n- The mean is 61.5 m and the median is 61.9 m.\n- The 5th to 95th percentile range is 46.5 to 75.0 m.\n\n**Slope**\n\nThe tool returned slope values without units. I read them as radians, because the aspect output spans \u00b1\u03c0. The degree values below are my conversion.\n\n| Statistic | Radians | Degrees |\n|---|---|---|\n| Median | 0.074 | about 4.2\u00b0 |\n| Mean | 0.154 | about 8.8\u00b0 |\n| 95th percentile | 0.553 | about 31.7\u00b0 |\n| Max | 1.291 | about 74\u00b0 |\n\n**What this means**\n- Most of the area is gentle to moderate. Half of the cells are below about 4\u00b0 (roughly a 7% grade).\n- The distribution is skewed. The mean is about twice the median, and the 95th percentile is about 32\u00b0. A small share of the terrain is steep, probably rock outcrops and embankments, and the maximum may include DEM artefacts.\n- Aspect covers the full \u00b1\u03c0 range, so there is no single dominant slope direction in the summary.\n\nThe rendered terrain mesh (10 m resolution) shows the surface shape only. The statistics have no spatial breakdown, so I can't say which parts of the area are steep or flat. I can export the slope raster (obj_5f14d705) as a TIF or CSV if you want to map it. I can also rerun the analysis on a smaller area, such as a specific campus part, or at a finer resolution.", "operations": [{"at": "2026-10-19T23:45:12.289Z", "turn_id": "turn_225945c6", "session_id": "bb6c5943cff0", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "geocode", "operation": null, "params_hash": "ad5faefbe482eb39", "seconds": 0.001, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": [], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:45:13.395Z", "turn_id": "turn_225945c6", "session_id": "bb6c5943cff0", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "60eb5c049e03b34b", "seconds": 0.031, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": true, "object_refs": ["obj_1986c754"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:45:15.224Z", "turn_id": "turn_225945c6", "session_id": "bb6c5943cff0", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "builder.build_terrain_raster", "params_hash": "eb5308a5e592b2b7", "seconds": 0.132, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_ebf82aa5"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:45:15.364Z", "turn_id": "turn_225945c6", "session_id": "bb6c5943cff0", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "builder.build_terrain_surface_mesh", "params_hash": "6b8525c572de1c2c", "seconds": 0.268, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_37441e94"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:45:16.609Z", "turn_id": "turn_225945c6", "session_id": "bb6c5943cff0", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "builder.raster.slope_aspect", "params_hash": "5a5e9a8c890ef70a", "seconds": 0.071, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_5f14d705", "obj_c83b181c"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:45:16.634Z", "turn_id": "turn_225945c6", "session_id": "bb6c5943cff0", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "render_object", "operation": null, "params_hash": "c46018a07550de71", "seconds": 0.096, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_37441e94"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}
{"question_id": "q09-too-large", "run": 2, "cache": "warm", "status": "ok", "error": null, "latency_s": 9.98, "provenance": {"at": "2026-10-19T23:45:33.195Z", "turn_id": "turn_41368e1b", "session_id": "9b766df75f64", "subject": "anonymous", "model": "eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5", "models_used": ["eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5"], "prompt_version": "a9f7e88fc432", "memory_context": false, "sdk": "pydantic-ai-slim 2.54.0", "tools_called": ["geocode", "run_operation"], "num_turns": 3, "duration_ms": 9671, "duration_api_ms": null, "total_cost_usd": 0.01586409, "usage": {"input_tokens": 8, "output_tokens": 996, "cache_read_input_tokens": 24409, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 802}, "is_error": false, "retried_fresh": false, "refused": false, "error": null, "http_status": null, "runtime": "pydantic-ai", "provider": "bedrock", "cost_source": "genai-prices 0.1.13 (regional.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5)"}, "images": 0, "files": 0, "answer": "I couldn't download the full 5 km \u00d7 5 km area (25 km\u00b2). The tool allows at most 10 km\u00b2 per download, because LiDAR data at that size needs several GB of memory. Nothing was downloaded.\n\nThe geocoder also placed \"Central Gothenburg\" at G\u00f6teborg Central station, around EPSG:3006 (319676, 6400380). I centered the 5 km box there.\n\nHere are three ways to go ahead:\n\n1. **One 3 km \u00d7 3 km square** (9 km\u00b2) around the station. This is the quickest option and covers the core of the city centre.\n2. **Four 2.5 km \u00d7 2.5 km tiles** (6.25 km\u00b2 each). Together they cover the full 5 km \u00d7 5 km. You'd get four separate point clouds, which are slower to fetch and use more memory. I'd run them one after another.\n3. **A smaller area around specific places**, such as Haga, Lindholmen or Chalmers.\n\nWhich would you like? If you don't mind, I'll start with option 1.", "operations": [{"at": "2026-10-19T23:45:25.335Z", "turn_id": "turn_41368e1b", "session_id": "9b766df75f64", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "g